; expect 70
; `IO.todo` at run time, in exactly the shape AX3005's quickfix
; writes: an arm `((Rect _ _) (todo "Rect"))` per missing constructor,
; the function tagged `;@axiom:effect(io)` because `todo` exits.
;
; `(todo "Rect")` types as `Int` here because the other arm does, and
; is never returned from: `main` builds a `Rect`, the arm is hit, the
; process writes `todo: Rect` to standard error and exits 70 - which
; is what `; expect 70` reads. The `Circle` arm is the control: a
; program that reached it would answer 4 and this case would fail.
(import IO (todo))

(data Shape
  (Circle Int)
  (Rect Int Int)
  (Dot))

(:: area (-> Shape Int))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (area s)
  (match s
    ((Circle r) (* r r))
    ((Rect _ _) (todo "Rect"))
    ((Dot) (todo "Dot"))))

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main) (area (Rect 1 2)))
